## How to use this library

This is reference, not a procedure. The phase skills (`video-brief`,
`video-story`, …) say which file to read; you can also read one when a
question comes up mid-job ("how do I make this scene feel tense?"). Read
the one file you need, not the library. Each file ends with what it means
in VertX.

## The files

| File | Read it when |
|---|---|
| `sections/short-form.md` | Writing or cutting anything under ~90 s: reels, shorts, ads; the hook, retention, one idea |
| `sections/screenwriting.md` | Writing scenes and dialogue: structure, scene craft, lines people can say |
| `sections/series.md` | Planning a series or writing an episode: arcs, the bible, cliffhangers, continuity |
| `sections/formats.md` | The shape of a documentary, explainer, ad, adaptation or podcast |
| `sections/styles.md` | Picking a look, writing the prompt prefix, the comic recipe |
| `sections/characters.md` | Designing and casting characters, keeping faces the same, casting voices |
| `sections/cinematography.md` | Shot sizes, angles, camera movement, composition, lenses, light, colour |
| `sections/directing.md` | Staging, performance in pictures, tone and genre |
| `sections/choreography.md` | Dance, fights, groups, and motion built from stills, cut to music |
| `sections/sound.md` | Directing voices, narration, music by function, effects and ambience, the mix |
| `sections/editing.md` | Cuts (match, J/L, jump, smash), pace and rhythm, transitions, montage, trailers |
| `sections/finishing.md` | Captions, titles, lower thirds, end cards, colour, the final check, versions |
| `sections/production-design.md` | Places, props, costume, the colour script, era and culture, continuity |
| `sections/podcast.md` | The show, the episode, interviews, hosts, editing speech, show notes, video podcasts |
| `sections/platforms.md` | Sizes, lengths, safe zones, thumbnails, loudness, posting (dated; check before promising a limit) |
| `sections/rights.md` | Music, pictures, faces and voices, AI labels, claims, credits |

The library grows when a real job shows a gap; platform numbers are dated
and rechecked.
